course: dictionary
lesson: 720
title: One word, two meanings: baron
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A baron is a noun, a person. Long ago it meant a nobleman of the lowest rank, a lord who held land from the king in the Middle Ages. «In 1215 English barons forced King John to agree to Magna Carta» shows barons as lords powerful enough to make a king listen.
explain: Today the news often uses baron for a very rich, powerful businessman who controls a big industry, such as an oil baron or a media baron. Context tells you which meaning is meant. If the sentence is about a king, a castle or a law, think history. If it is about money, oil or newspapers, think business.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence in place of the word. Does «a powerful businessman who controls newspapers» fit «a media baron»? If yes, you have chosen the right meaning.
fact: A baron is a noun. A woman with this rank is a baroness.
fact: In history, a baron was a nobleman of the lowest rank in Britain, or a lord who held land from the king in the Middle Ages.
fact: In 1215 English barons forced King John to accept Magna Carta, which said that even the king must obey the law.
fact: In the news, a «baron» can be a very rich, powerful businessman in one industry, such as «an oil baron» or «a media baron».
fact: A «drug baron» is a powerful criminal boss.
exercise: In 1215 English barons forced King John to agree to Magna Carta. What kind of barons were they? | Shop owners in London | *Powerful lords who held land from the king | Children from a school | Visitors to a museum
exercise: «The oil baron bought three more companies this year.» What does baron mean here? | A noble lord who held land | A pirate on a ship | A wise old king | *A very rich and powerful businessman
exercise: What does «drug baron» mean? | *A powerful criminal boss | A ship's captain | A kind man who gives money to the poor | A doctor who makes medicine
test: Priya reads «the media baron bought a newspaper». Which meaning of baron fits? | A criminal in prison | A nobleman in the Middle Ages | *A powerful businessman who controls newspapers | A lord who ruled a castle
test: Which word is the female form of baron? | Barrel | *Baroness | Barren | Barona
exam: Read «In 1215 barons forced King John to accept Magna Carta, saying even the king must obey the law.» Which clue shows barons here means powerful lords, not businessmen? | *The king and Magna Carta in 1215 show it is history | The word oil shows it is about business | The word media shows it is about newspapers | Barons always mean criminals
